From a810de2ef9644b9b145acc1c53ccdcf3f69533b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:14:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(theme): accent tints follow --odon-accent

~100 button tints, active states and focus rings hard-coded the default
blues (rgba(59,123,255,..); rgba(96,165,250,..) in dark mode) and greens
(rgba(18,185,129,..)), so a theme accent only recoloured part of the UI.

They are now color-mix() tints of --_odon-accent, a new --_odon-accent-dark
(dark-theme accent, defaults to the old #60a5fa) and --_odon-accent2, with
the stock colours as defaults: the default look is unchanged. The .dark and
.dark .odontogram-root blocks re-resolve the accents so a nested dark scope
can carry its own --odon-accent. Perio data colours are untouched.

New public --odon-accent-fg (default #fff) is the text on solid-accent
controls (active Status/Plan and perio switches, furcation and Miller
grades), so a light accent keeps readable labels.

Also fixes the dark-mode perio-overlay switch: a later .dark rule with the
same specificity wiped the active background (dark text on a near-black
chip); the active switch now uses the dark accent.

Tests: accent-colours.test.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
